claim.claim-text:
9. A method of forming a screw fastener blank using a header die a method of forming a screw fastener blank using a header die, the blank being of the type having: (i) a head portion and a tip portion; 

 (ii) a noncircular cross section with an axis and a plurality of circumferen- tially spaced radial lobes and valley portions between the radial lobes, said noncircular cross section having an out-of-round attribute K which is a difference between a first maximum radial dimension measured from the axis to a peak of a radial lobe and a second least radial dimension measured from the axis to a lowest valley portion, said method comprising using a forming die cavity including walls for forming: (a) a main body portion of the screw fastener blank adjacent to the head portion and being of a predetermined diameter; (b) a tapered thread-forming-section adjacent the tip portion and of diameter which tapers down from said predetermined diameter towards said tip portion said die cavity having a first predetermined value of K for the main body portion, and a second value of K for the tapered thread forming section, said second value of K being greater than said first predetermined value of K; said die cavity including: (c) an additional thread forming section located between the main body portion and the tapered thread-forming-section and being of axial length capable of accommodating at least one thread, said addi- tional thread forming section having the same predetermined diameter as said main body portion and having substantially the same value of K as the tapered thread forming section; the method including the step of using: a selectively positionable knock-out pin that stops linear movement of the blank beyond a predetermined axial point during for- mation, the knock-out pin being constructed and arranged to selectively uncover and reveal a stabilizing section forming die cavity axially for- ward of a part of the die cavity that forms the tapered thread-forming section, the stabilizing section forming die cavity being constructed 

 i and arranged to form a blank stabilizing section with a lower stabiliz- 2 ing lobe maximum diameter than the main body lobe maximum di- 3 ameter.
